As you can see on the right, in case of Docker,&nbsp;
we have the underlying hardware, infrastructure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.450 --> 00:09:45.180
and then the OS and then Docker installed on&nbsp;
the OS. Docker then manages the containers that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.180 --> 00:09:50.370
run with libraries and dependencies alone.&nbsp;
In case of virtual machines, we have the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.370 --> 00:09:56.580
