evolved over time, and now supports a lot more&nbsp;
options than it did in the beginning. For example,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:28:37.340 --> 01:28:44.570
this is the trimmed down version of the Docker&nbsp;
compose file we used earlier. This is in fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:28:44.570 --> 01:28:51.830
the original version of Docker compose file known&nbsp;
as version one. This had a number of limitations.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:28:51.830 --> 01:28:59.270
For example, if you wanted to deploy containers on&nbsp;
a different network other than the default bridge&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:28:59.270 --> 01:29:05.000
network, there was no way of specifying&nbsp;
that in this version of the file. Also,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:29:05.000 --> 01:29:11.030
say you have a dependency or startup order of some&nbsp;
kind. For example, your database container must&nbsp;&nbsp;

