01:30:44.090 --> 01:30:51.050
automatically creates a dedicated bridged network&nbsp;
for this application, and then attaches all&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:30:51.050 --> 01:30:58.670
containers to that new network. All containers are&nbsp;
then able to communicate to each other using each&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:30:58.670 --> 01:31:05.150
other's service name. So you basically don't need&nbsp;
to use links in version two of Docker compose,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:31:05.150 --> 01:31:12.050
you can simply get rid of all the links you&nbsp;
mentioned in version one when you convert a&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:31:12.050 --> 01:31:19.401
file from version one to version two. And finally,&nbsp;
motion to also introduces a depends on feature.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:31:19.400 --> 01:31:25.850
If you wish to specify a startup order. For&nbsp;
instance, say the voting web application is&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:31:25.850 --> 01:31:31.940
dependent on the Redis service. So you need to&nbsp;
ensure that Redis container is started first,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:31:31.940 --> 01:31:38.270
and only then the voting web application must&nbsp;
be started. We could add a depends on property&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:31:38.270 --> 01:31:47.120
to the voting application and indicate that it&nbsp;
is dependent on Redis. Then comes version three,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:31:47.120 --> 01:31:54.170
which is the latest as of today. version three&nbsp;
is similar to version two in the structure,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:31:54.170 --> 01:31:59.330
meaning it has a version specification at the top&nbsp;
and the Services section under which you put all&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:31:59.330 --> 01:32:06.260
your services just like in version two, make sure&nbsp;
to specify the version number as three at the top.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:32:06.260 --> 01:32:13.940
version three comes with support for Docker swarm,&nbsp;
which we will see later on. There are some options&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:32:13.940 --> 01:32:19.670
that were removed and added. To see details on&nbsp;
those you can refer to the documentation section&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:32:19.670 --> 01:32:25.820
using the link in the reference page. Following&nbsp;
this lecture. We will see version three in much&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:32:25.820 --> 01:32:33.440
detail later, when we discuss about Docker&nbsp;
stacks. Let's talk about networks in Docker&nbsp;&nbsp;

