is a background process that manages Docker&nbsp;
objects such as the images, containers, volumes&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:40:21.800 --> 01:40:28.850
and networks. The Docker REST API server is the&nbsp;
API interface that programs can use to talk to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:40:28.850 --> 01:40:35.240
daemon and provide instructions, you could create&nbsp;
your own tools using this REST API. And the Docker&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:40:35.240 --> 01:40:40.880
CLA is nothing but the command line interface&nbsp;
that we've been using, until now to perform&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:40:40.880 --> 01:40:47.690
actions such as running a container stopping&nbsp;
containers, destroying images, etc. It uses&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:40:47.690 --> 01:40:55.700
the REST API to interact with the Docker daemon.&nbsp;
Something to note here is that the Docker CLA need&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:40:55.700 --> 01:41:02.810
not necessarily be on the same host. It could be&nbsp;
on another system like a laptop, and can still&nbsp;&nbsp;

